, and in knowledge, and in all manner of workmanship;¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse ¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙJand to devise curious works, to work in gold, and in silver, and in brass,¦layout ªlast_verse „¥verse!¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙfand in the cutting of stones, to set them, and in carving of wood, to make any manner of cunning work.¦layout ªlast_verse!„¥verse"¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙpAnd he hath put in his heart that he may teach, both he, and Aholiab, the son of Ahisamach, of the tribe of Dan.¦layout ªlast_verse"„¥verse#¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÚThem hath he filled with wisdom of heart, to work all manner of work, of the engraver, and of the cunning workman, and of the embroiderer, in blue, and in purple, in scarlet, and in fine linen, and of the weaver, even of them that do any work, and of those that devise cunning work.¦layout ªlast_verse#